I really like this game. Just battling, leveling up, collecting equipment and recruiting battlers. If you cannot write a good story or just don't want to write a story, you can follow what this game has done.
Pros:
1. Very deep RPG-maker combats (traditional turn based combat). The game nearly utilize all what RPG-maker can provide;
2. You can build you characters in different ways (physical or magic);
3. You can see your characters are getting stronger step by step, little by little;
4. Many other interesting elements like catching bats, random chests and crafting, etc.
Cons:
2 major things:
1. The combat pace is too slow, if the battle speed can be doubled, that would be nice. Maybe the developers can add 2 items in options: (1) adjust combat speed and (2) not to see the animation in combat. If so, it can largely improve the game experience;
2. The BP system. Many BP skills seems powerful, but it is quite hard to gain BP during the combat, so it will lead to nearly 90% BP skills I have never used because I want to save BP for those more powerful skills. Most of Henry's skills are BP skills, so most of time Henry is normal attacking.
Generally speaking, I recommend this game and I really hope the developers can finish this game in a good way.
Good luck!
